; @electron-forge/plugin-fuses@7 declares a stale peer range (@electron/fuses@^1)
; but works with the @electron/fuses@2 this repo pins. This was a repo-wide
; `legacy-peer-deps=true`, which nub refuses (ERR_NUB_UNSUPPORTED_CONFIG: it always
; resolves peers). The conflict is now pinned narrowly instead, in the `overrides`
; block of package.json, so npm and nub agree on one graph. See ADR 0039.

; Electron Forge addresses node_modules by flat literal path -- forge.config.ts
; PACKAGE_KEEP_PREFIXES keeps `/node_modules/node-addon-api`, which is a transitive
; dependency. nub defaults to an isolated symlink store where that path does not
; exist and `nub run make` fails outright, so force the flat npm-style tree.
; npm does not recognise this key and warns; that noise is the accepted cost of a
; single install layout for both tools. See ADR 0039.
node-linker=hoisted

; nub holds a 24h cooling window over registry resolutions, and by default fails
; hard when the only matching version is younger than that. The `doctor` script
; runs `react-doctor@latest`, which the code-review policy mandates, so a
; same-day release of that tool would block the gate outright. Degrade to the
; newest *mature* version instead of erroring; the cooling protection is kept.
; (`minimumReleaseAgeExclude` is the documented per-package escape hatch but is
; not honored on the `nubx`/`dlx` path in nub 0.6.0.)
minimumReleaseAgeStrict=false
